WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.033
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.534
You're here!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.334
Thank you for watching.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.200
Well, guys,
let's get to some news.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.100
Today, Chinese President
Xi Jinping met virtually

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.601
with Russian President
Vladimir Putin.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.067
They didn't talk even.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:21.968
They just spent an hour
exchanging maniacal laughter.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:25.834
[ Laughing evilly ]

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:28.467
It's not great news for Biden.
I mean, for Marvel fans,

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.334
it's like if Spider-Man
found out that Doc Ock

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:31.801
was Zooming
with the Green Goblin.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.167
I mean, something is happening.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.934
But they had a lot to discuss,
like trade, nuclear arms,

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:39.400
and why Carrie
didn't call 9-1-1.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:43.501
At one point,
Xi called Putin his old friend,

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:46.934
and Putin called Xi
his dear friend.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.200
Then they ended the call like,
"You hack us first,"

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.300
"No, you hack us first!"
"Oh, no, you hack us first!"

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:56.601
Some big news in Washington.
The House voted to hold

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:59.100
former Trump chief of staff
Mark Meadows

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.467
in criminal contempt of Congress
for refusing to cooperate

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.601
with the January 6th panel.

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:06.601
The consequences are severe.
Meadows could be sentenced

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.400
to a year in prison,
or, even worse,

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.834
another month working for Trump.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:13.400
Of course,
Meadows needs a good lawyer,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.667
so the first thing he did
was pull up

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:16.667
Rudy Giuliani's number
and delete it.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:21.033
Some more news.
The White House just announced

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.400
that, due to COVID concerns,

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.501
instead of the traditional
holiday parties,

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:27.200
he's inviting guests
to come see the decorations

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.734
on a 30-minute self-guided tour.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.901
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.868
Which is just a fancy way
of Biden saying,

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.501
"Come if you want,
but I ain't gonna be there."

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:37.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:39.400
"I ain't getting COVID."
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.000
So guests can now go
on a 30-minute self-guided tour

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.501
of an old mansion.

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:44.634
There's actually a name
for that --

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:47.400
it's called a haunted house.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.734
That's right.
A self-guided tour

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:50.400
of a historic
Washington building.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:53.300
That's basically how Fox News
described January 6th.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:58.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.968
Listen to this -- I heard that
pharmacists across the country

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:03.567
are feeling burned out
due to increased demand

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:07.100
for COVID shots
and being short-staffed.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.067
Yeah, I'm sure it's that
and not just hearing

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.133
The Chipmunks Christmas on loop
for two months.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:14.167
It's like, "I'm losing it, Gary.
I'm losing it.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.968
Get him a hula hoop!
Get them a hula hoop!"

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.567
You know your pharmacist
is stressed out

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:20.734
when they disinfect your arm

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:23.067
with the Bacardi
from their flask.

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:25.267
"Shot for you, shot for me,
right?"

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:26.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:28.801
It's gotten so bad now,
when you order Xanax,

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:31.000
the pharmacist says,
"We just ran out."

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:36.267
Get this.
In Canada, a 5-year-old is safe

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:38.734
after he was caught driving
his parents' car

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:41.167
to go buy a Christmas present
for his sister.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:42.767
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.968
The cop asked him to recite
the alphabet backwards,

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:46.868
and he was like, "I haven't even
learned it forwards."

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:49.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.133
Yeah, he's in a lot of trouble,

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.434
so, really, his sister got
the greatest gift of all.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:57.501
Meanwhile, the kid showed
each officer a packet

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:58.634
of Dunkaroos and said,

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:00.634
"How about we, uh,
say this never happened?"

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.834
And, finally, this is something
you don't hear every day.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:05.868
Authorities in Ohio
are investigating

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:09.100
after someone stole
a 58-foot bridge.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.300
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.934
Police say they're
on the lookout for a thief

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:13.634
who's described
as having dark hair,

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:15.634
blue eyes, and is the Hulk.

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.334
Guys, we have
exactly three shows left

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:18.767
before we go on Christmas break,

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:19.901
which means it's time
for that beloved

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.133
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:24.567
It's time for "12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters."

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:25.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:27.901
-♪ "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters" ♪

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:32.334
♪ Three days left ♪

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:33.400
-That is right.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.901
Every show between
now and Christmas,

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:38.133
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:40.067
an extraordinary
Christmas sweater

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:41.801
from our
Countdown to Christmas Cabinet.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:45.501
Yes!

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:48.667
Now, since there are
three shows left,

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.000
let's open door number 3.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.167
Where's 3? Oh, here.

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.968
When -- Whenever you're ready.
Go for it.

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:57.701
Whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.701 --> 00:03:59.367
Wait. Whoa, whoa, whoa. Yeah.
Let's see it.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.901
Oh. Wow.

00:04:02.901 --> 00:04:07.133
Oh, that is -- That is...
That is something.

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:08.567
Can we dim the lights
a little bit?

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:11.567
Maybe that's --
Look at this thing. Ooh, yeah.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:12.734
That's like...

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:14.133
Show the back to them?

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:15.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:17.767
That is space age.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:20.100
That is space age.
Wow. Fantastic.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.367
Now, let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:23.634
Everyone, look at
your seat number.

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:25.868
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:27.834
Quest, can I get
a drum roll, please?

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:32.934
[ Drum roll ]

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:35.000
242!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.667
Hi!

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.834
Welcome! Hi! Welcome!

00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:45.434
Come on over!

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.701
Aw, look at you.

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:49.934
Hello. What is your name?

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:51.501
-Karina.
-Karina, where are you from?

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:53.534
-Jersey.
-Yeah! Jersey!

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.767
All right, good.
Karina from Jersey.

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:57.767
You already look like
you're in the holiday spirit.

00:04:57.767 --> 00:05:00.667
I love the -- But I think that
this will just kind of go

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.934
with everything.
-I love it.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.701
-Yeah.
-I love it.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.467
-No one -- You won't stand out
in Jersey if you wear this.

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:07.367
-I know. I'm gonna
go to dinner in this.

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:08.667
-You should.
Would you like to try it on?

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:09.968
-Can I?
-Yes, please.

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:11.968
I think we'd love to see it.
This is gonna be amazing.

00:05:11.968 --> 00:05:13.601
I think it's gorgeous.

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:15.100
There...

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.300
♪♪

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.534
Yeah. It's easy to get on.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:20.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.567
Look at this.
Are you kidding me?

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Are you joking me?

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:27.234
Yo. Karina, look at you.
You're...

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:29.467
That looks like
a super model on our show.

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:31.400
It's unbelievable.
Gorgeous.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.767
Thank you so much for
being here! I appreciate it.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:35.100
Another round of applause
for our winner.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.300
You can leave if you want.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.267
You can stay.
Whatever you feel like doing.

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:39.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Round of applause

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:41.100
for our winner right there.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.267
Stick around!

00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:43.667
We got more "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:45.133
Come on back, everybody.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:52.634
♪♪

